  "term": "amaurosis fugax",
  "definition": "Amaurosis fugax is a brief episode of complete or partial vision loss in one eye caused by reduced blood flow to the retina. It is often linked to material such as emboli traveling into the central retinal artery, commonly from the carotid artery.",
